From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 16:26:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Guard attachment path templating against NULL values

gowhatsapp_attachment_fill_template() substitutes placeholders through
replace_placeholder(), which passes the hash table value straight to
purple_strreplace(). Some values can be NULL - an unset buddy or chat
alias, or a missing filename or extension, e.g. for a message we sent
ourselves from another device whose recipient is not in the buddy list.
purple_strreplace() then fails its 'replacement != NULL' assertion and
returns NULL, the template result becomes NULL, and the NULL path later
crashes in g_path_get_dirname() / create_symlinks_recurse(), taking the
whole libpurple process down.

Substitute an empty string for a NULL value, stop replacing once the text
is NULL, and make create_symlinks_recurse() return on NULL paths.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 glue/handle_attachment.c | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/glue/handle_attachment.c b/glue/handle_attachment.c
index 5dfef98..664d173 100644
--- a/glue/handle_attachment.c
+++ b/glue/handle_attachment.c
@@ -129,8 +129,15 @@ static void download_via_xfer_mechanism(gowhatsapp_message_t *gwamsg) {
 
 static void replace_placeholder(gpointer key, gpointer value, gpointer user_data) {
     char **text = user_data;
+    // A NULL replacement value (e.g. an unset alias, filename or extension) must NOT reach
+    // purple_strreplace: it asserts 'replacement != NULL', returns NULL, nulls *text, and the
+    // resulting NULL path later crashes g_path_get_dirname. Coalesce NULL to "" and skip once
+    // *text is NULL.
+    if (*text == NULL) {
+        return;
+    }
     // NOTE: I am not using g_string_replace here since the GLib shipped with win32 Pidgin is ancient
-    char *replaced = purple_strreplace(*text, key, value);
+    char *replaced = purple_strreplace(*text, key, value ? (const char *)value : "");
     g_free(*text);
     *text = replaced;
 }
@@ -177,7 +184,7 @@ char * gowhatsapp_attachment_fill_template(const char *template, time_t timestam
 // TODO: for a cross-platform-solution, check out https://github.com/nyaosorg/go-windows-junction
 void create_symlinks_recurse(char *path, char *aliased_path) {
     //purple_debug_info(GOWHATSAPP_NAME, "create_symlinks_recurse(%s, %s)…\n", aliased_path, path);
-    if (strlen(path) <= 1 || strlen(aliased_path) <= 1) {
+    if (path == NULL || aliased_path == NULL || strlen(path) <= 1 || strlen(aliased_path) <= 1) {
         // we reached / or . – stop recursion
         return;
     }
